<%# The contact form. It lives here (a plain-ERB partial) rather than in the Contentful `contact`
    page body because that body is rendered through markdown_to_html → Redcarpet SmartyPants
    (lib/helpers/markdown_helpers.rb), which curls the straight quotes in raw HTML *attributes*
    and so corrupts the form's field names + Stimulus wiring. The intro copy above the form stays
    editable in Contentful; this partial is appended for the contact page in
    partials/article/_body.html.erb.

    Keep the field names (name, email, message, honeypot `comment`) in sync with the api's
    Api::ContactController — see the root CLAUDE.md contact contract. Progressive enhancement: the
    real method/action work without JS (native POST → 303 to /contact/success); the `contact`
    Stimulus controller intercepts submit to fetch + toast when JS is present. %>
<form method="POST" action="/api/contact" class="form"
      data-controller="contact" data-action="submit->contact#submit" data-turbo="false">
  <wa-input label="Your name" type="text" name="name" autocomplete="name" with-clear required></wa-input>
  <wa-input label="Your email" type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" with-clear required></wa-input>
  <label class="hp">Comment <textarea name="comment" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off"></textarea></label>
  <wa-textarea label="What's on your mind?" name="message" rows="6" resize="auto" with-count required></wa-textarea>
  <wa-button type="submit" variant="brand" appearance="accent" data-contact-target="submit">
    Send Message
    <%= icon_svg("classic", "solid", "paper-plane")&.sub("<svg", '<svg slot="end"') %>
  </wa-button>
</form>
